<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/windward-oahu.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/windward-oahu-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/windward-oahu.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="900" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.1"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><a href="/island-communities/">Island communities</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><span aria-current="page">Kailua &amp; Kaneohe</span></nav><p class="tag">Oahu · Windward Oahu</p><h1>Insurance Appraiser for Kailua and Kaneohe Homes</h1><p class="lede">Trade-wind rain, stream flooding and the occasional severe thunderstorm make Windward Oahu claims distinct. We help Kailua and Kaneohe owners resolve disputes over what a repair really costs.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn sun" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn line-light" href="/contact-hawaii-appraiser/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="facts"><div><dt>County</dt><dd>City and County of Honolulu</dd></div><div><dt>Island</dt><dd>Oahu</dd></div><div><dt>Service</dt><dd>On-site inspections</dd></div></dl></div></section><div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose"><div class="local"><div><b class="h">Local claim risks</b><ul class="chips"><li>Heavy rain and stream overflow</li><li>Trade-wind and Kona storm wind</li><li>Rare hail and severe storms</li><li>Roof and plumbing leaks</li></ul></div><div><b class="h">Neighborhoods we cover</b><ul class="chips soft"><li>Kailua town</li><li>Lanikai</li><li>Enchanted Lake</li><li>Maunawili</li><li>Kaneohe</li><li>Ahuimanu</li><li>Kahaluu</li><li>Waimanalo</li></ul></div><p><b>Housing:</b> Windward Oahu is mostly single-family homes from the 1950s onward, with beachfront houses, valley homes under the Koolau cliffs, townhome complexes and a growing number of ohana units.</p><p><b>History:</b> A March 2012 supercell over Windward Oahu produced the largest hailstone on record in Hawaii, and heavy rain events and Kona lows have repeatedly flooded low-lying streets and streams.</p></div>
<h2>Living and building on the windward side</h2>
<p>Kailua and Kaneohe sit on the wet side of the Koolau Range, where trade winds push moisture against the cliffs nearly every day. That climate shapes the houses. Kailua is largely single-family neighborhoods – from beach cottages near Lanikai to 1960s homes around Enchanted Lake and Maunawili. Kaneohe climbs from the bay into Ahuimanu and toward Kahaluu, with hillside lots, townhome complexes and homes that have been expanded over the decades with ohana units for extended family.</p>
<p>Constant moisture means roofs, gutters and wood framing work hard here. It also means insurers often look for wear, rot or termite activity when a claim comes in, which can turn a straightforward storm claim into a disagreement over cause and scope.</p>
<h2>Windward storm history</h2>
<p>The windward side is where Hawaii saw one of its most unusual weather events: a March 2012 supercell thunderstorm that dropped the largest hailstone ever recorded in the state. Hail remains rare, but the event showed that severe storms can strike here. More routinely, heavy rain overwhelms streams and drainage channels, and Kona lows can bring wind from the south and west, catching roofs and windows from an unexpected direction.</p>
<h2>Common Windward Oahu disputes</h2>
<ul>
<li>Roof claims where the carrier blames age, UV exposure or salt air instead of wind.</li>
<li>Water intrusion through windows and walls during wind-driven rain, and whether interior damage is “long-term seepage.”</li>
<li>Mold remediation limits applied to losses that were reported promptly.</li>
<li>Repairs to additions and ohana units priced at lower quality than the main house.</li>
<li>Rising-water damage, which is generally excluded unless you carry separate flood insurance.</li>
</ul>
<div class="note"><b class="h">Know your flood coverage</b>Most homeowners policies exclude surface water and flood. If stream water entered your home, check whether you carry an NFIP or private flood policy before assuming your homeowners carrier will pay.</div>
<h2>How appraisal fits Windward claims</h2>
<p>Appraisal is useful when coverage is accepted but the dollar amount is not. If your insurer agrees a storm damaged your roof but offers a patch where you need a replacement, or prices interior repairs well below local contractor bids, the appraisal clause may let a neutral process set the amount. It does not decide whether a loss is covered; denials and coverage disputes belong with a Hawaii attorney.</p>
<p>Hawaii Insurance Appraiser documents roof condition, measures slopes and squares, and prices work at Windward Oahu labor and material rates, including freight and General Excise Tax. Our <a href="/appraisal-specialties/roof-hail-claim-appraisal/">roof and hail claim appraisal</a> service covers storm roofs, and the <a href="/island-claim-tools/roof-pitch-squares-estimator/">roof pitch and squares estimator</a> gives you a quick way to check the measurements in your carrier’s estimate. You can also read our guide on <a href="/hawaii-claim-guides/salt-air-corrosion-vs-storm-damage/">salt air corrosion vs. storm damage</a>.</p>
<p>If you are unsure where to begin, gather your policy, the carrier’s estimate, dated photos and any contractor bids. With those in hand, we can usually tell you quickly whether the gap between the numbers is large enough to make appraisal worthwhile for your Windward home.</p>
<h2>Specialties available in Kailua &amp; Kaneohe</h2><p>Every Hawaii Insurance Appraiser specialty is available to owners and associations in Kailua &amp; Kaneohe, including:</p><ul class="cols2"><li><a href="/appraisal-specialties/appraisal-clause-representation/">Appraisal Clause Representation</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-specialties/homeowner-claim-appraisal/">Homeowner Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-specialties/condo-aoao-commercial-appraisal/">Condo, AOAO &amp; Commercial</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-specialties/roof-hail-claim-appraisal/">Roof &amp; Hail Claims</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-specialties/kona-storm-high-wind-claims/">Kona Storm &amp; High-Wind Claims</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-specialties/hurricane-claim-appraisal/">Hurricane Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-specialties/water-damage-claim-appraisal/">Water Damage Claims</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-specialties/fire-smoke-claim-appraisal/">Fire &amp; Smoke Claims</a></li></ul>
<h2>Questions from Kailua &amp; Kaneohe owners</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Hail is rare in Hawaii. Will my insurer take a Windward Oahu hail claim seriously?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="a"><p>It should evaluate the claim on the evidence. Severe storms with hail have occurred on the windward side, so clear photos, dates and an inspection soon after the storm help support the claim.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is wind-driven rain through a window covered on the windward side?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="a"><p>Many policies cover interior water damage when wind first creates an opening in the roof or walls, but wording varies. Read your policy’s windstorm and water provisions or ask a Hawaii attorney if coverage is denied.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can appraisal cover damage to an ohana unit on my Kaneohe property?<svg class="chev" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="a"><p>If the ohana unit is insured under your policy and the loss is covered, its repair cost can be part of the amount the appraisers determine. Detached structures may fall under a separate other-structures limit.</p></div></details></div>
<h2>Nearby communities</h2><div class="related"><a href="/island-communities/honolulu-oahu/"><small>Nearby</small><span>Honolulu</span><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a href="/island-communities/mililani-wahiawa-oahu/"><small>Nearby</small><span>Mililani &amp; Wahiawa</span><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a href="/island-communities/pearl-city-aiea-oahu/"><small>Nearby</small><span>Pearl City &amp; Aiea</span><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></div></article><aside class="aside"><div class="box box-call"><h2 class="box-t">Talk it through first</h2><p>The first conversation is free. We’ll tell you plainly whether appraisal fits your claim.</p><a class="big" href="tel:+18445371427">+1 (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn sun" href="/contact-hawaii-appraiser/">Send claim details</a><small>Mon–Fri 7am–5pm HST</small></div><div class="box"><h2 class="box-t">Island communities</h2><ul class="box-list"><li><a href="/island-communities/honolulu-oahu/">Honolulu</a></li><li><a href="/island-communities/kailua-kaneohe-oahu/" aria-current="page">Kailua &amp; Kaneohe</a></li><li><a href="/island-communities/pearl-city-aiea-oahu/">Pearl City &amp; Aiea</a></li><li><a href="/island-communities/kapolei-ewa-beach-oahu/">Kapolei &amp; Ewa Beach</a></li><li><a href="/island-communities/mililani-wahiawa-oahu/">Mililani &amp; Wahiawa</a></li><li><a href="/island-communities/hilo-big-island/">Hilo</a></li><li><a href="/island-communities/k